questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput payment processing engine intermittently fails to roll back database transactions during unexpected runtime exceptions. Additionally, thread dumps show multiple threads executing concurrently without creating isolated transactional contexts.

Here is the snippet from the backend service:
java
@Service
public class PaymentProcessor {

    @Autowired
    private PaymentRepository paymentRepo;

    public void processBatch(List<Payment> payments) {
        payments.parallelStream().forEach(this::processPayment);
    }

    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    public void processPayment(Payment p) {
        paymentRepo.save(p);
        if (p.isInvalid()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid payment payload");
        }
    }
}
